
== §1 — SPEC INTEGRITY AND NO-DRIFT ==
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_visual.json
  ✓ schema and compiler version are pinned
  ✓ all nine visual modes are declared
  ✓ every material is classified VISUAL_MATERIAL and nothing else
  ✓ no material in the library carries an engineering property
  ✓ material provenance separates SYSTEM_DEFAULT from USER
  ✓ the spec forbids treating a render as measured or as-built
  ✓ the spec names no code, standard or authority
  ✓ the AI may not change any layout feature

== §2 — NO ENGINEERING GEOMETRY MUTATION ==
  ✓ compiling a scene mutates no source model
  ✓ every visual mode leaves the model untouched
  ✓ every discipline model is byte-identical after visualisation
  ✓ every theme leaves the compiled architecture identical
  ✓ every quality profile leaves the compiled architecture identical
  ✓ the summary states no engineering geometry was modified
  ✓ no scene contains a geometry-generation or redesign claim

== §3 — OBJECTS ARE DERIVED, NEVER AUTHORED ==
  ✓ every non-visual object names the model element it came from
  ✓ every source element id resolves in the architectural model
  ✓ wall count in the scene equals the wall count in the model
  ✓ opening count in the scene equals the opening count in the model
  ✓ an object sized from a render fallback says so
  ✓ no display fallback is relabelled as a model dimension
  ✓ the visual roof cap is visual-only and never a modelled roof
  ✓ a model that states a roof gets no visual cap

== §4 — VISUAL MODES ==
  ✓ every declared mode compiles
  ✓ an unknown mode falls back to PRESENTATION rather than inventing one
  ✓ ENGINEERING mode shows every discipline
  ✓ ENGINEERING mode is still available and technically styled
  ✓ ARCHITECTURAL mode applies finishes rather than technical shading
  ✓ ARCHITECTURAL mode adds ceilings that ENGINEERING mode omits
  ✓ PRESENTATION mode carries a sky, exposure and tone mapping
  ✓ every mode reports the same model hash for the same model

== §5 — MATERIALS AND PROVENANCE ==
  ✓ every emitted material is VISUAL_MATERIAL
  ✓ no emitted material carries a fire, thermal or structural property
  ✓ a material chosen by the system is SYSTEM_DEFAULT, not a user requirement
  ✓ a material chosen by a theme is VISUAL_THEME, not a user requirement
  ✓ a material stated by the user is USER
  ✓ an AI-suggested material stays AI_SUGGESTED
  ✓ an unknown material never silently becomes a real one
  ✓ a material name is never treated as an engineering material

== §6 — THEMES CHANGE APPEARANCE ONLY ==
  ✓ a theme changes the finishes it selects
  ✓ a theme changes no room dimension, opening or level
  ✓ an unknown theme falls back to the default rather than inventing one
  ✓ a theme never changes the building type or level count

== §7 — DECORATION IS NOT ENGINEERING DATA ==
  ✓ decoration is emitted only when explicitly requested
  ✓ every decoration object is VISUAL_ONLY and never semantic
  ✓ no decoration object references a model element
  ✓ decoration is excluded from the engineering export
  ✓ decoration appears only in an explicitly requested presentation export
  ✓ a user-requested object stays engineering data and is never re-labelled
  ✓ decoration never enters an occupant, coverage or load count
  ✓ decoration counts are reported separately from semantic objects
  ✓ entourage is visual-only and never an occupant

== §8 — SITE, LANDSCAPE AND WATER ==
  ✓ a stated site produces a ground plane at the stated size
  ✓ a model with no site still renders, and says the extent is not a boundary
  ✓ the ground plane is always visual-only
  ✓ landscape objects are visual-only and separately layered
  ✓ water is emitted only for a represented water feature
  ✓ no pool is ever invented in any fixture
